+---
+type: decision
+status: active
+updated: 2026-11-03
+sources: [.harness/gate-shrink-detail.md, .harness/spike-bprime/RESULTS.md, 3556e27, 0be020e, 732af47, 6f606e5, c4a72dd, 0011]
+verified_by: tests/gate.test.sh
+---
+# 0012: Shrink the conductor gate, keep it a script
+
+**Context.** The "4b" item (gate shrink, [0005](0005-gate-only-inside-herdr.md)) asked for `permissions` rules plus a ≤50-line gate. The analyst's inventory (`.harness/gate-shrink-detail.md` §2-3) found a 552-line gate. Replaying 881 real conductor Bash calls (2026-10-18..10-28) gave 754 allowed, 127 denied (106 from two ungated sessions). Allowed usage was `harness`, `cat`/`ls` under `.harness|docs`, `git log|status|diff --stat|branch`, `gh pr create|merge|view|edit|list|comment|checks`, and `herdr pane current|get`. Never used: `git show --stat`, `herdr status|pane list|layout|workspace|tab`, `gh issue|run|repo|auth|browse|pr status`, and jq as a pipe consumer (0 allowed). Chaining with `;`/`&` was 44 of 754 (5.8%), pipes 0. No filesystem MCP server was configured.
+
+The B′ spike (native subagents instead of the harness runner) was rejected on 2026-11-03 (`.harness/spike-bprime/RESULTS.md`): subagents die when the conductor exits ("1 local agent couldn't be moved and was stopped"), so detached `claude -p` workers stay ([0011](0011-single-runner-headless.md)) and so does the gate that confines the conductor.
+
+**Decision.** Keep the gate as a bash script and cut it to observed use, in steps that each kept `tests/gate.test.sh` green:
+- Single-command scanner (`scan_command`, one simple command per call), `agent_type` keying, and `tests/gate-denied.list` (every probe must stay denied, controls allowed): done before this step.
+- Allowlist trimmed to usage (3556e27): `gh pr create|view|list|checks|comment|edit|merge` only (`--body-file` from `.harness/` or `docs/`, no `pr merge -d`, no `api`); `git branch` list-only (`-a -r -v --show-current`); `herdr pane get|current`; no `jq`, no `git show`.
+- Dead tool cases dropped (0be020e): `Agent`, `Workflow`, `Monitor`, `NotebookEdit` and the `mcp__filesystem__*` block are gone from the gate; `claude/agents/conductor.md` `disallowedTools` carries the first four, and the hook matcher is `Edit|Write|Read|Grep|Glob|Bash`.
+- Policy tables (`MSG_*`, `BASH_ALLOW`, `GH_ALLOW`, `GIT_DENY`) moved into one labelled block at the top (6f606e5), so policy edits do not touch parser code.
+- `--via` no-op removed from `harness ask` (732af47); an unknown option is refused (exit 1) without starting a run.
+- Gate tests added for each form listed under "You may run directly" in `conductor.md`, plus deny probes for the dropped forms (c4a72dd).
+
+**Kept, and why.** The path helpers (`rel`, `physrel`, `physical`, `readable`, `writable`) and the quote-aware scanner and character allowlist stay: they are what stops `Read bin/harness`, `..`, symlinks from `docs/` into source, raw `.harness/log/*.jsonl` streams and chaining, and they carry most of the review-fix tests. The Bash allowlist stays an allowlist, not a deny list: anything unlisted (`python3`, `sed`, `herdr pane run`) is denied by default.
+
+**Rejected: option f, `permissions` rules instead of the script.** Rules live in user-scope `~/.claude/settings.json`, so they also bind the workers (headless `claude -p` sessions of the same user), which must read and edit source. Only a hook can key on `agent_type` (conductor vs worker) and on the harness checkout (0010). Path symlink resolution and `--body-file` checks also have no rule syntax.
+
+**Status.** Active. The gate is 520 lines (552 at the analysis, 513 before the policy header); the 50-line target of 0005's critique is dropped.
+
+**Consequences.** Supersedes the 4b consequence in 0005 (gate shrink via permissions). A new conductor command form needs a line in the policy block, a gate test, and a line under "You may run directly" in `conductor.md`. The gate is a live file: `bash -n` and the gate suite before every save ([live-gate-edit](../troubleshooting/live-gate-edit.md)). The deny text did not change, so [conductor-shell-one-command](../troubleshooting/conductor-shell-one-command.md) is unchanged.
